**Accepted deferred implementation.** Runtime anonymous records are planned and
are not yet executable in the Alpha compiler.

An anonymous record groups local values without declaring a named type:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    show_window ||:
        window ~= (
            title = "Strategy",
            size = (width = 1280, height = 720),
        )

        window.size.width = 1440
    ;
]

Every field needs a name and a value. Records can nest directly. Runtime fields
may use ordinary runtime expressions and follow normal access and copy rules.

Each literal site has its own hidden nominal type. Matching fields do not make
two different sites interchangeable. Use explicit constructors for named types.

The initial feature is local-only. Records carrying hidden types cannot be
passed to functions, returned, exported or stored in collections or maps.
Ordinary values extracted from their fields follow their normal rules.

See @../constants/#const-records (Const records) for compile-time member groups
and @../language-overview/#mon-syntax (MON syntax) for the shared notation.
